    "inputHash": "sha256:653bf8d8accd97b516138f573f3b54308e205019eadd1baf77ce70220d7c0e72",
    "notes": "The model reproduces the 600 m sandstone gravity wall, 80 low sluices and 72 upper arched apertures, plus the crest railway, traveling gantry, embankments and two irrigation intakes. The PMTiles crest rail establishes the signed placement. Two local grades tie the retained rail approaches to the model. The Blue Nile uses a representative 421.7 m reservoir and 410.3 m tailwater. A 416 m canal stage leaves both intake gates visible. The fixed crest and water stages are representative estimates from retained maps, standard terrain and photos. The canal levels, embankment shoulders and gantry position are approximate. The sluices are static. Terrain corrections depend on the host serving the Protomaps semantic IDs and height samples fine enough to resolve the graded shoulders."
  },
